$ grep ERROR
Every stage: optimized retrieval.

$ awk '$3 == "ingest-stream:" { print HOST, $0 }' | grep 'first row'
Every stage: optimized retrieval.

$ awk '$3 == "x" { printf "%s\n", $0 }' | grep y
  1  awk '$3 == "x" { printf "%s\n", $0 }'  partly optimized
       pattern: optimized; action: post-retrieval
       Action does more than print the line or its fields.
       Try: Print only, e.g. `print $1, HOST`.
  2  grep y                                 post-retrieval

Barrier: stage 1. Everything after it: post-retrieval.

$ awk '$NF > 10 { print $1 }'
  1  awk '$NF > 10 { print $1 }'  post-retrieval
       Computed field position ($NF, $i).
       Try: Use a fixed position ($1, $2), or jq on a JSON source.

Barrier: stage 1. Everything after it: post-retrieval.

$ awk 'BEGIN { FS = "," } { print $2 }'
  1  awk 'BEGIN { FS = "," } { print $2 }'  post-retrieval
       BEGIN can change line splitting.
       Try: Drop BEGIN; use awk's default splitting.

Barrier: stage 1. Everything after it: post-retrieval.

$ awk -F, '{ print $2 }'
  1  awk -F, '{ print $2 }'  post-retrieval
       Flag -F, changes line splitting.
       Try: Fixed separator: `cut -d<sep> -f<n>` is optimized (lines without the separator pass whole).

Barrier: stage 1. Everything after it: post-retrieval.

$ tr a b | grep y
  1  tr a b  post-retrieval
       tr: post-retrieval only.
  2  grep y  post-retrieval

Barrier: stage 1. Everything after it: post-retrieval.

$ grep y | tr a b
  1  grep y  optimized retrieval
  2  tr a b  post-retrieval
       tr: post-retrieval only.

Barrier: stage 2. Everything after it: post-retrieval.

$ sort -n | grep y
  1  sort -n  post-retrieval
       No optimized form.
  2  grep y   post-retrieval

Barrier: stage 1. Everything after it: post-retrieval.

$ jq -s 'length'
  1  jq -s 'length'  post-retrieval
       -s reads the whole stream as one input.

Barrier: stage 1. Everything after it: post-retrieval.

$ jq 'select(.a == 1) | .b | tostring | ascii_downcase'
  1  jq 'select(.a == 1) | .b | tostring | ascii_downcase'  partly optimized
       select: optimized; rest: post-retrieval
       After the selects: more than picking fields.

Barrier: stage 1. Everything after it: post-retrieval.

$ sed 's/a/b/'
  1  sed 's/a/b/'  post-retrieval
       sed optimized only as `sed -n '/re/p'`.
       Try: Matching lines: use grep. Substitution: post-retrieval, so put it after narrowing stages.

Barrier: stage 1. Everything after it: post-retrieval.

$ cut -d, -f1,3-
Every stage: optimized retrieval.

$ grep -e a -e b
  1  grep -e a -e b  post-retrieval
       grep optimized with -i, -v, or no flags; not -e.

Barrier: stage 1. Everything after it: post-retrieval.

$ tail -n 100 /log/acme/api/main.log | grep y
  1  grep y  post-retrieval
       Filters rows a head or tail already kept.
       Try: Filter first: that gives the last N matches, not the matches among the last N.

Barrier: stage 1. Everything after it: post-retrieval.

